description:
The `html_vignette` template currently uses a folded YAML block:

```yaml
vignette: >
  %\VignetteIndexEntry{Vignette Title}
  %\VignetteEngine{knitr::rmarkdown}
  %\VignetteEncoding{UTF-8}
```

R scans these directives as physical source lines. However, YAML defines newlines inside `>` as foldable, so a YAML formatter may validly combine the last two lines without changing the YAML value. This causes R to misread the vignette encoding during `R CMD check`.

Could the template use a literal block instead?

```yaml
vignette: |
  %\VignetteIndexEntry{Vignette Title}
  %\VignetteEngine{knitr::rmarkdown}
  %\VignetteEncoding{UTF-8}
```

`|` is more accurate because it makes the required line boundaries part of the YAML value and prevents semantics-preserving formatters from combining the directives.

I have followed [this issue](https://github.com/rstudio/rmarkdown/issues/1384) in order to render a rmarkdown to pdf while using `kableextra`, but It fails when I'm using the shiny app. If I use the `Knit` button from Rstudio IDE, it will compile, but not from the shiny app !
I have prepared a minimal example as well : 

```
library(shiny)
library(dplyr)
library(kableExtra)

ui <- fluidPage(
  sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
      numericInput("n_rows", label = "Number of rows to display", value = 10),
      downloadButton('report',"Generate Report")
    ),
    mainPanel(
      tableOutput("mtcars_table")
    )
  )
)


server <- function(input, output,session) {
  output$mtcars_table <- renderTable({
    head(mtcars, n = input$n_rows)
  })
  
  output$report <- downloadHandler(
    # For PDF output, change this to "report.pdf"
    filename = "report.pdf",
    content = function(file) {
      withProgress(message = 'Calculation in progress',{
        incProgress(session = session)
        tempReport <- file.path(tempdir(), "report.Rmd")
        file.copy("report.Rmd", tempReport, overwrite = TRUE)
        
        params <- list(df = mtcars[input$n_rows,])
        
        rmarkdown::render(tempReport, output_file = file,
                          params = params,
                          envir = new.env(parent = globalenv())
        )
        incProgress(session=session)
      }, session = session)
    }
  )
}


shinyApp(ui, server)  
```

