I recently started working with parameterized reports as documented [here](https://rmarkdown.rstudio.com/developer_parameterized_reports) and wrote some shiny apps that let users set  parameters in the GUI, render the document with an `actionButton` and then view/download the rendered document.

It would be very handy to generate the GUI elements for the parameters automatically from the yaml header like `knit_params_ask` does. I began working on a [shiny module](https://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/modules.html) that aims at doing exactly this. The module currently looks as follows

```r
paramsUI <- function(id, file) {
  ns <- NS(id)
  params <- knitr::knit_params(readLines(file))
  lapply(names(params), function(name) {
    param_ui(params, name, ns)  
  })
}

paramsServer <- function(input, output, session, file) {
  params <- knitr::knit_params(readLines(file))
  ## return reactive value containing the modified params
  reactive({ 
    getParams(input, params) 
  })
}
```

where `param_ui` generates the UI for one of the parameters and `getParams` modifies the inputs to match the requirements of `rmarkdown::render(..., params = params)`. A full example can be found in [this gist](https://gist.github.com/GregorDeCillia/3601ebaf8f285d4e37bfd8f69c8f4b4f).

So my request would be to include a similar module in the `RMarkdown` package and using the module as a backend of `knit_params_ask`. IMO, the easiest way to do this is to recreate the above module based on the source code of `knit_params_ask`. I could submit a PR soon if there is interest from the `RMarkdown` devs.

